15 0 obj
<< /A 50 0 R /Alt (Five strawberries in different ripeness stages: unripe \(green\),breaker-stage \(light green with hints of red\), half-ripe \(more red\), commercially-ripe\(mostly red\), and fully-ripe \(near-complete or full red coverage.\).) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 35 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 51 0 R /Alt (Four images of strawberries at different ripeness stages, with bounding boxes and percentage labels indicating ripeness. Strawberries vary from green and unripe to red and ripe.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 36 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 52 0 R /Alt (Diagram illustrating a neural network model with two branches: Attention and Downsample. The Attention Branch involves Average Pooling, Convolution, Rearrange, and Softmax processes. The Downsample Branch uses Group Convolution and Rearrange. Both branches output to combine features through element-wise multiplication and addition, producing the final output.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 37 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 53 0 R /Alt (Diagram illustrating a neural network structure with three layers labeled P5, P4, and P3. P5 \(green\) is 13x13, P4 \(pink\) is 26x26, and P3 \(blue\) is 52x52. Arrows indicate data flow and operations including upsampling \(UP2\) and downsampling \(DS2\). C3k2_Star nodes and fusion nodes are included. Outputs are labeled P5_out, P4_out, and P3_out.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 38 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 54 0 R /Alt (Flowchart of the C3K2_Star Module. It includes an input image of strawberries passing through a series of Star_Blocks with convolutional layers \(Conv 1x1\), and shortcut paths. The process involves element-wise multiplication, denoted by an asterisk, with operations like DW-Conv 7x7, F1 and F2: Conv 1x1, ReLU6 activation, G: Conv 1x1, Batch Normalization \(BN\), and DW-Conv 7x1, culminating in the addition operation.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 39 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 55 0 R /Alt (Flowchart of a neural network architecture for object detection, showing three main sections: Backbone, Neck, and Head. The Backbone involves convolution layers \(Conv\), LAWDS, and C2PSA modules. The Neck includes fusion and upsampling operations with C3K2_Star modules. The Head features detection layers outputting feature maps of sizes 52, 26, and 13. An input image of a fruit basket is resized at the top left.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 40 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
21 0 obj
<< /A 56 0 R /Alt (Precision-recall curve illustrating the performance of different classes in fruit ripeness detection. Classes include unripe, breaker stage, half ripe, commercially ripe, fully ripe, and all classes combined. The unripe class shows the highest average precision at 0.974, while commercially ripe has the lowest at 0.748. The overall mean average precision for all classes is 0.886. Precision and recall range from 0.0 to 1.0 along the axes.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 42 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
22 0 obj
<< /A 57 0 R /Alt (Normalized confusion matrix for fruit ripeness classification. Rows represent predicted classes: unripe, breaker stage, half ripe, commercially ripe, fully ripe, background. Columns represent true classes. Values indicate prediction accuracy per class.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 42 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
23 0 obj
<< /A 58 0 R /Alt (Line graph showing mAP50 performance over epochs for different\nmodels: RTDETR-l, YOLOv5s, YOLOv8n, YOLOv10n, YOLO11n, YOLO12n, LBS-YOLO.\nLBS-YOLO \(red line\) achieves the highest performance. The mAP50 of the LBS-YOLO model is significantly higher than the other models in the figure.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 44 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
24 0 obj
<< /A 59 0 R /Alt (Bar chart comparing model performance based on metrics mAP50 and mAP50-95 for different models: RTDETR-l, YOLOv5s, YOLOv8n, YOLOv10n, YOLOv11n, YOLOv12n, and LBS-YOLO. LBS-YOLO shows the highest performance with mAP50 at 0.871 and mAP50-95 at 0.746, while RTDETR-l scores lowest. Error margins are indicated.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 45 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
25 0 obj
<< /A 60 0 R /Alt (Comparison of object detection models on strawberry images in three panels, P1, P2, and P3. The models include SSD, Faster R CNN, EfficientDet, RTDETR-I, YOLOv8n, YOLOv10n, YOLO12n, YOLO11n, and LBS-YOLO. Each model displays a varying accuracy in identifying ripe strawberries, highlighted with boxes and confidence scores. Some are marked with red crosses or green checks to indicate errors or correct detections.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 46 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
26 0 obj
<< /A 61 0 R /Alt (Original and thermal images showing strawberries with detectionboxes using two methods, Baseline and LBS-YOLO. The baseline image's attention is quite scattered, while the LBS-YOLO heatmap is more compact, fits the edges better, and shows a stronger ability to grab the target's meaning.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 47 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
